; Regression: `print go(1)` as the LAST statement emitted nothing at rc 0
; (2026-10-04). An operand sequence reads left to right, so this is
; `(print go)(1)`: the collapse leaves an "operator" call carrying the
; FUNCTION's name. One statement earlier the effect-free gate refused it
; (`xfail_parenless_chain_dropped` is the member shape); the last statement was
; judged only where the operator had NO name, because a block's last statement
; may be its value -- and a call under a function's name is never one.
; Measured before: `define i32 @main() { ret i32 0 }`.
;
; xfail: the result of operator 'go' is discarded

function go(n: int) returns String
    String#("x")

print go(1)
